<title>SWEDEN: S-E-Banken posts 17 pct rise in Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>S-E-Banken posts 17 pct rise in Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank S-E-Banken on Tuesday posted these earnings for the first quarter of the year ending on March 31.</p>
<p>				    (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,498 vs 1,278</p>
<p> Loan losses				   165 vs   433</p>
<p> Net interest income		     2,244 vs 1,535</p>
<p> Operating costs			   2,336 vs 2,073</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	     1,663 vs 1,711</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,498 vs 1,278</p>
<p> Tax					     347 vs   229</p>
<p> Capital adequacy ratio (pct)	  12.20 vs 11.37</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				 2.38 vs  2.06</p>
<p>Net equity (March 31, 1997 vs  March 31, 1996)			  22,555 vs 18,821</p>
<p>NOTE - Swedish commercial bank S-E-Banken was expected to post a first quarter operating profit after credit losses of 1.38 billion crowns, a Reuter poll of 11 analysts showed.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
